\f0\b \cf2 Changes in this FW:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 	\'95	Push buttons can now be mapped to pins. They will work the same as the PS/2 keyboard keys\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}This FW actually has all the pins mapped for my new 10 button keypad, which does double duty as a numpad\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}But you can leave the numpad code in the FW and just change the pins, it should be fine\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}+/- now has hold down mode so you can scroll through feed values\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Decimals are stable, always 2 in metric, always 3 in imperial (I hope). \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}If you use my custom screenset this means the values don\'92t jump left and right when jogging\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Long pressing the Left Stop (Limit) deletes all limits. This has now been moved to FW from the Nextion side. \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}RPM, Turns, Angle now consolidated into one box, so the value can be shown larger. You toggle between them by tapping the value. You can also turn this font green by long pressing the small RPM/Turns/Angle text\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Increments change color depending on their value - red for the coarsest, then yellow, then green \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Since I can\'92t decide on which font to use for the Pitch text box, you can swap between three fonts by tapping the box\
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
